foundation.question_text:
The graph shows two accounts, each opened with $\$4000$ at $10\%$ p.a. One pays simple interest and the other compounds annually.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=7.8cm,height=5.8cm,axis lines=left,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=9.2,ymin=0,ymax=9500,xtick={0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8},ytick={0,2000,4000,6000,8000},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\scriptsize,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={Years},ylabel={Balance (\$)},title={Two accounts, $\$4000$ at $10\%$ p.a.}]
\addplot[thick,blue,dashed,domain=0:8,samples=2]{4000+400*x};
\addplot[thick,red,domain=0:8,samples=60]{4000*exp(x*ln(1.1))};
\node[blue,right,font=\small] at (axis cs:8,7200) {$A$};
\node[red,right,font=\small] at (axis cs:8,8574) {$B$};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Which line shows the simple interest account, and what is that account's balance after $5$ years?

foundation.solution_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=7.8cm,height=5.8cm,axis lines=left,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=9.2,ymin=0,ymax=9500,xtick={0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8},ytick={0,2000,4000,6000,8000},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\scriptsize,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={Years},ylabel={Balance (\$)},title={Two accounts, $\$4000$ at $10\%$ p.a.}]
\addplot[thick,blue,dashed,domain=0:8,samples=2]{4000+400*x};
\addplot[thick,red,domain=0:8,samples=60]{4000*exp(x*ln(1.1))};
\node[blue,right,font=\small] at (axis cs:8,7200) {$A$};
\node[red,right,font=\small] at (axis cs:8,8574) {$B$};
\draw[dashed,gray] (axis cs:5,0)--(axis cs:5,6000)--(axis cs:0,6000);
\node[above right,font=\scriptsize] at (axis cs:0.2,6000) {$\$6000$};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Line $A$ is a straight line, so the balance grows by the same amount every year: this is the simple interest account.
Reading line $A$ at $5$ years gives a balance of $\$6000$.

development.question_text:
Offer A pays $8\%$ p.a. simple interest and Offer B pays $6.5\%$ p.a. compounding annually, on a deposit of $\$5000$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=7.8cm,height=5.8cm,axis lines=left,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=13.4,ymin=0,ymax=11500,xtick={0,2,4,6,8,10,12},ytick={0,2000,4000,6000,8000,10000},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\scriptsize,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={Years},ylabel={Balance (\$)},title={Offer A and Offer B on $\$5000$}]
\addplot[thick,blue,dashed,domain=0:12,samples=2]{5000+400*x};
\addplot[thick,red,domain=0:12,samples=60]{5000*exp(x*ln(1.065))};
\node[blue,right,font=\small] at (axis cs:12,9800) {$A$};
\node[red,right,font=\small] at (axis cs:12,10645) {$B$};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the first whole year in which Offer B is ahead of Offer A.

development.solution_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}\begin{axis}[width=7.8cm,height=5.8cm,axis lines=left,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=13.4,ymin=0,ymax=11500,xtick={0,2,4,6,8,10,12},ytick={0,2000,4000,6000,8000,10000},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\scriptsize,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={Years},ylabel={Balance (\$)},title={Offer A and Offer B on $\$5000$}]
\addplot[thick,blue,dashed,domain=0:12,samples=2]{5000+400*x};
\addplot[thick,red,domain=0:12,samples=60]{5000*exp(x*ln(1.065))};
\node[blue,right,font=\small] at (axis cs:12,9800) {$A$};
\node[red,right,font=\small] at (axis cs:12,10645) {$B$};
\draw[dashed,gray] (axis cs:8,0)--(axis cs:8,8275);
\node[font=\scriptsize,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (axis cs:8,2600) {$n=8$};
\end{axis}\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Offer A: $5000+400n$
Offer B: $5000(1.065)^{n}$
$n=7$: $\$7800$ and $\$7769.93$, so A is ahead.
$n=8$: $\$8200$ and $\$8274.98$, so B is ahead.
Offer B is first ahead after $8$ years.
